, "e": 5.168}, {"text": "Every samurai wore a pair of blades called a daisho: the long katana for open battlefield combat, and the shorter wakizashi for indoor fighting where low ceilings made a long sword useless.", "s": 5.348, "e": 19.742}, {"text": "Only the samurai class was legally permitted to carry both weapons, making the pair an instant badge of rank.", "s": 19.862, "e": 27.565}, {"text": "Even when visiting a friendly lord's house and leaving their katana at the door, a samurai kept the short sword tucked in their sash.", "s": 27.685, "e": 36.747}]}